        " رَجُلٍ أَكَلَ مِنْ لَحْمِ صَيْدٍ لَا يَدْرِي مَا هُوَ وَ هُوَ مُحْرِمٌ قَالَ عَلَيْهِ دَمُ شَاةٍ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Muhammad Bin Yahya, raising it, ",
          "(It has been narrated) from Abu Abdullah<sup>asws</sup> regarding a man who ate from the flesh of a hunted prey not knowing what it was, and he was in <span class=\"iTxt\">Ihraam</span>. He<sup>asws</sup> said: ‘Upon him is blood of a sheep’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "7. Muhammad ibn Yahya has narrated from in a marfu‘ manner the following: “About a man who in the state of Ihram eats of the flesh of a prey and does not know what it is, abu ‘Abd Allah, ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ’He owes one sheep.’” "
        ]
      }
